From 93c9d3fa98302570bcc4ffd58b81e61128946c30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Waschkeit <44188360+HarryWaschkeit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 09:56:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] net: fec: fix unbalanced clk disable when
 register_netdev() fails

fec_probe() explicitly disables the enet_out/ptp/ref/2x_txclk clock
group via fec_enet_clk_enable(ndev, false) once initialization has
completed, just before registering the netdev. However, if
fec_enet_mii_init() or register_netdev() subsequently fails, the
error unwind path falls through unconditionally to the
failed_clk_ipg label, which calls fec_enet_clk_enable(ndev, false)
a second time.

This double-disables clocks that are already off, which is caught
by the clk core and produces WARN_ON splats such as:

  WARNING: CPU: 3 PID: 37 at drivers/clk/clk.c:1181 clk_core_disable+0x1b0/0x1e0
  enet_phy already disabled
  ...
  WARNING: CPU: 3 PID: 37 at drivers/clk/clk.c:1040 clk_core_unprepare+0x20c/0x238
  enet_phy already unprepared

observed on a phyGATE-Tauri-L-iMX8MM when register_netdev() fails
with -EEXIST because a competing PCIe NIC (igb) has already claimed
the eth0 name that FEC1 is statically assigned via the 'ethernet0'
alias.

Track whether the clock group has already been suspended with a
local 'clks_suspended' flag and skip the redundant disable call in
the shared cleanup path if so.

Signed-off-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Harry Waschkeit <44188360+HarryWaschkeit@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fec_main.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fec_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fec_main.c
index 53c028c72234..33c58e9dd5e4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fec_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fec_main.c
@@ -4336,6 +4336,7 @@ fec_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	int irq_cnt;
 	struct fec_devinfo *dev_info;
 	int eth_id;
+	bool clks_suspended = false;
 
 	fec_enet_get_queue_num(pdev, &num_tx_qs, &num_rx_qs);
 
@@ -4548,6 +4549,7 @@ fec_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	/* Carrier starts down, phylib will bring it up */
 	netif_carrier_off(ndev);
 	fec_enet_clk_enable(ndev, false);
+	clks_suspended = true;
 	pinctrl_pm_select_sleep_state(&pdev->dev);
 
 	ndev->max_mtu = PKT_MAXBUF_SIZE - ETH_HLEN - ETH_FCS_LEN;
@@ -4590,7 +4592,8 @@ fec_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 failed_clk_ahb:
 	clk_disable_unprepare(fep->clk_ipg);
 failed_clk_ipg:
-	fec_enet_clk_enable(ndev, false);
+	if (!clks_suspended)
+		fec_enet_clk_enable(ndev, false);
 failed_clk:
 	release_bus_freq(BUS_FREQ_HIGH);
 failed_rgmii_delay:
-- 
